    <p>Hi Ruchi,<br>
      <br>
      Thank you for your email and for summarizing our recent
      discussion.<br>
      <br>
      I would like to clarify a few points to ensure that my
      understanding and the discussion are accurately reflected.<br>
      <br>
      Regarding the reference to <b>career growth, skill development,
        and capability enhancement</b>, I would like to clarify that I
      do not recall having a specific discussion regarding these areas
      or any particular skill-development or capability-enhancement
      requirements during our conversation. Therefore, I would
      appreciate it if you could please clarify the specific areas being
      referred to.<br>
      <br>
      Regarding the reference to <b>opportunities outside the
        organization and my personal business plans</b>, I had shared
      these points only as part of a general conversation about my
      future plans. My understanding was not that these were the basis
      for any decision regarding my employment or notice period.<br>
      <br>
      Regarding the statement that I <b>requested early relieving</b>,
      I would like to clarify the context of our discussion. When you
      mentioned that the company would provide a 30-day notice period
      and asked me to consider resignation for an early relieving, I
      shared my personal view that, if the company provides a <b>30-day
        notice period</b>, I would be open to requesting early relieving
      from my end, subject to the company's approval and feasibility of
      the handover.<br>
      <br>
      <br>
      At the same time, I also clearly mentioned that if early relieving
      is not possible, I am prepared to serve the applicable notice
      period as per my employment terms. I had also mentioned that,
      based on my understanding of the terms I signed during my last
      appraisal, the notice period may be <b>90 days</b>. Therefore, if
      I do not secure another opportunity during the initial period, I
      am prepared to serve the applicable notice period as per the
      agreed terms.<br>
      <br>
      Regarding the transition timeline, before confirming my last
      working date, I would request the company to <b>please confirm
        the notice period applicable to my employment</b>. If the
      applicable notice period is <b>90 days</b>, I am prepared to
      serve the same, particularly if I do not receive another
      opportunity before the proposed 30-day timeline.<br>
      <br>
      I would also appreciate clarification on the following:<br>
      <br>
      1. What notice period is currently applicable to my employment?<br>
      2. Is the applicable notice period <b>45 days as mentioned in my
        appointment letter</b>, or <b>90 days as per the terms I signed
        during my last appraisal?</b><br>
      3. Could you please share a copy of the relevant document/terms
      signed during my last appraisal so that I can review and
      cross-confirm the applicable terms and conditions?<br>
      <br>
      I have reviewed my appointment letter, and my understanding is
      that it mentions a <b>45-day notice period</b>. However, I recall
      that a revised or additional agreement/bond was signed during my
      last appraisal, which I believe mentioned a <b>90-day notice
        period</b>. I would therefore appreciate it if you could share
      the relevant document for confirmation.<br>
      <br>
      Once the applicable notice period is confirmed, I will be able to
      provide my expected last working date accordingly and coordinate
      the required handover to ensure a smooth and professional
      transition.<br>
      <br>
      Thank you for your understanding and support.<br>
      <br>
      Regards,<br>
      Rahul</p>
