      <meta http-equiv="content-type" content="text/html; charset=UTF-8">
      <div dir="ltr">
        <div>Hi Rahul,<br>
          <br>
          <p>As discussed during our recent conversation regarding your
            career growth and current role expectations, we also
            discussed certain areas where further improvement in skill
            development, and capability enhancement would be required to
            support your continued growth within the organization. We
            understand that, considering these aspects, you have been
            evaluating opportunities outside the organization, along
            with your personal business plans.<br>
            <br>
            During the discussion, you also expressed your willingness
            to move on from the organization and requested an early
            relieving, considering the offers you currently have in
            hand. We appreciate the openness and transparency with which
            you shared your thoughts and future plans with us.</p>
          <p>Accordingly, rather than moving forward with discussions
            around your current role expectations and
            performance-related processes, we would like to understand
            your preferred timeline for transition and relieving. This
            will help us plan the necessary work handover and ensure a
            smooth transition for both you and the organization.</p>
          <p>Please let us know your expected last working date or the
            earliest date by which you would like to be relieved. </p>
          <p>We will review your requested date based on business
            requirements, project commitments, and the required
            handover, and we will try our best to facilitate the
            transition at the earliest possible date.</p>
          <p>We value your contribution and want to ensure a
            professional and respectful transition.</p>
          <p>For any further clarification regarding the terms and
            conditions of your employment, please refer to your
            appointment letter.</p>
          <p><br>
          </p>
          <p><br>
          </p>
        </div>
